<title>HONG KONG: Hopewell fiscal 1996 net down 63 pct.</title>
<headline>Hopewell fiscal 1996 net down 63 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hopewell Holdings Ltd reported on Thursday a net profit of HK$769.19 million for the year ended June 30, 1996 compared with net profit of HK$2.1 billion a year earlier.  </p>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   17.6	  vs 48.3</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    3.0	   vs 10.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  223.89 gain vs 1,529.81 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    769.19	vs 2,100.16</p>
<p>    Turnover		     2,365.18    vs 2,175.96</p>
<p>    Company name		 Hopewell Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  November 9-14</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   November 18</p>
<p>NOTE - Hopewell Holdings is an investment holding and property investment and development company.</p>
<p>Net is after exceptional item on income from sale of electricity generated by the Shajiao C Power Station ahead ofits scheduled completion date.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is six H.K. cents (including interim dividend of three cents) vs 20 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
